> From: Elijah Gabe Pérez <eg642616@gmail.com>
> Date: Fri, 18 Jul 2025 19:34:51 -0600
> 
> Is there a way to use another mode than fundamental-mode for files
> without a file extension or without an available major mode?

The node "Choosing Modes" in the Emacs user manual describes all the
facilities we have in Emacs to specify a major mode for a file.  Most
of the facilities do not require any special file-name extensions, but
can match arbitrary file names without extensions.

